From 2121f8cefd2b286b6aee1db7f6d662ae0e22c262 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artyom Shalkhakov <artyom.shalkhakov@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 08:06:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NSControl, NSCell: typing undone on the editing's own undo
 manager

What was typed into a text field could not be undone: every cell's
allowsUndo was NO unless set, and keyed decoding never read it (a xib's
cells came out NO whatever the xib said).  And a field editor that did
allow undo, a custom one say, registered its typing on its window's
undo manager, which is usually a document's, where it does not belong;
one that groups only when told to raises on it.

On macOS 15 every cell allows undo unless told not to (NSCell,
NSActionCell, NSTextFieldCell, NSButtonCell, NSFormCell...), a xib's
cell does unless it says allowsUndo="NO", and keyed archiving keeps the
setting.  While a field is edited, its field editor's undo manager is
one of the cell's (an NSCellUndoManager), not the window's: the window's
gets no typing, Undo in the field undoes the typing, and the next field
edited starts with nothing to undo.

So a cell allows undo from -initTextCell:, -initImageCell: and keyed
decoding, which reads the flag -encodeWithCoder: already writes
(NSCellFlags2 0x1000); the xib unarchiver sets that flag from
allowsUndo="NO"; and NSControl answers -undoManagerForTextView: for its
field editor with an undo manager of the editing's own, made when the
editing first asks and dropped when it ends.

Tests/gui/NSCell/allowsUndo.m (4 of its 5 checks fail without the
change), Tests/gui/NSControl/editingUndo.m (5 of 10) and
Tests/gui/GSXib5KeyedUnarchiver/cellUndo.m with CellUndo.xib (1 of 3)
check each of these; with the change they pass, and so does the rest of
the gui suite.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
